{"slug": "endive-and-apple-salad", "nyt_id": 1014356, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014356-endive-and-apple-salad", "name": "Endive and Apple Salad", "author": "Tara Parker-Pope", "description": "This salad came to The Times from Kathryn Anible, a personal chef in New York, whose solution to adding color to your winter table lies in this fresh, crunchy salad. “I just like it because the endive is not frequently used in salads, and it tends to be a little bitter,” she said. “The apple sweetens it up a little bit and makes it more approachable. It has a nice crunchy, fresh texture.” Tara Parker-Pope", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "PT20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "¼ cup olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 tablespoons apple cider vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "apple cider vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 tablespoon orange juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "orange juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 teaspoon honey", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "honey", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Dash of salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "dash of salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "¼ cup pecans", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "pecans", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 heads of endive, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "head", "item": "of endive", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 cup arugula", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "arugula", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 apple, sliced thin", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "apple", "preparation": "sliced thin", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¼ cup dried cherries or cranberries", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "dried cherries or cranberries", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "¼ cup goat cheese, crumbled (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "goat cheese", "preparation": "crumbled (optional)", "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "To make dressing: In a small bowl, whisk together the oil, vinegar, juice and honey. Season with salt."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a small sauté pan, toast the pecans over medium heat. Allow to cool."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Mix together the endive, arugula, apple and cherries (or cranberries) in a medium-size bowl. Toss with enough dressing to coat. Top with the pecans and goat cheese (optional)."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 251.25, "protein_g": 3.2, "carbohydrates_g": 15.2, "fat_g": 20.5, "saturated_fat_g": 3.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.9, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 5.2, "sodium_mg": 94.6, "fiber_g": 2.3, "sugar_g": 11.2, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["salad"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["apple", "fall", "pecan", "thanksgiving"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2012/11/20/health/wellveggie_leafy2/wellveggie_leafy2-superJumbo-v3.jpg", "alt": "Endive and apple salad", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2012/11/20/health/wellveggie_leafy2/wellveggie_leafy2-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "Endive and apple salad", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 249}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2012-11-20", "scraped_at": "2026-09-